-- title:
--   Section ideal on a fibre component: invertible of degree one
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $C$ a scheme and $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a separated morphism; let $U \subseteq C$ be an open subscheme whose structure morphism $U \hookrightarrow C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $\sigma$ be a section of $c$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ with $\sigma$ followed by $c$ the identity, whose set-theoretic image lies in $U$. Let $k$ be a field and $t : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a morphism, and write $\mathrm{rigSection}\,c\,t\,\sigma : \operatorname{Spec} k \to C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} k$ for the induced point of the base change, namely the map with components $t$ followed by $\sigma$ and the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} k$; `sectionIdeal c σ t` is its kernel ideal sheaf. Let $J$ be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on the base change, with associated closed immersion $J.\mathrm{subschemeι}$, and assume there is an affine open $V$ of the base change containing the image of $\mathrm{rigSection}\,c\,t\,\sigma$ with $J(V) = 0$. Then: (i) the inverse image of `sectionIdeal c σ t` along $J.\mathrm{subschemeι}$ is invertible in the project's sense, that is, every point of the closed subscheme cut out by $J$ has an affine open neighbourhood of the form a basic open $D(f)$ inside some affine open on which the ideal is generated by a single non-zero-divisor; (ii) the composite of the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by this inverse-image ideal, the closed immersion $J.\mathrm{subschemeι}$, and the projection $\mathrm{pr}_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$ is a finite morphism; and (iii) for every point $q$ of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ the `finrank` of that composite at $q$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that a section passing through the smooth locus meets a fibre component containing its reduction in a single reduced $k$-rational point: the restricted section ideal is an effective Cartier divisor of degree one on the component. It is the one-section input to the computation of Euler characteristics, hence multidegrees, of line bundles built from divisors supported on sections of a resolved model.
